WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.567 --> 00:00:02.168
-Well,

00:00:02.168 --> 00:00:04.771
last night, we all watched
a petulant psycho

00:00:04.771 --> 00:00:06.939
debase himself
and the nation on live TV

00:00:06.939 --> 00:00:08.941
and, now,
his deranged sycophants

00:00:08.941 --> 00:00:11.410
are making all kind of excuses
for his performance.

00:00:11.410 --> 00:00:13.480
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:18.317
[ Suspenseful theme plays ]

00:00:18.317 --> 00:00:21.354
So, where to begin
with that debate last night?

00:00:21.354 --> 00:00:23.456
Actually, debate
is not the right word.

00:00:23.456 --> 00:00:25.491
It was more like a collective
brain hemorrhage.

00:00:25.491 --> 00:00:27.994
It was like watching
democracy get a lobotomy

00:00:27.994 --> 00:00:29.261
or, as CNN put it...

00:00:29.261 --> 00:00:30.763
-This was the most chaotic

00:00:30.763 --> 00:00:32.765
presidential debate
I've ever seen

00:00:32.765 --> 00:00:34.433 line:0%
and I suspect most of you,

00:00:34.433 --> 00:00:36.302 line:0%
if not all of you,
have ever seen.

00:00:36.302 --> 00:00:39.138 line:0%
-That was a hot mess

00:00:39.138 --> 00:00:41.040 line:0%
inside a Dumpster fire,

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:42.876 line:0%
inside a train wreck.

00:00:42.876 --> 00:00:45.678 line:0%
That was the worst debate
I have ever seen.

00:00:45.678 --> 00:00:48.281 line:0%
In fact,
it wasn't even a debate.

00:00:48.281 --> 00:00:49.782 line:0%
It was a disgrace.

00:00:49.782 --> 00:00:51.151 line:0%
-That was a [bleep]show.

00:00:51.151 --> 00:00:53.652 line:0%
And, you know, we're on cable.
We can say that.

00:00:53.652 --> 00:00:56.856 line:0%
Apologies for being,
maybe, a little bit crude.

00:00:56.856 --> 00:00:58.358
-You guys are being
way too charitable.

00:00:58.358 --> 00:01:01.394
Watching that debate was like
hotboxing a Porta Potti

00:01:01.394 --> 00:01:02.662
with crystal meth

00:01:02.662 --> 00:01:04.630
in Phoenix, in July.

00:01:04.630 --> 00:01:07.233
It was like being hit
on the head with a lead pipe

00:01:07.233 --> 00:01:08.968
in a room filled
with nitrous oxide.

00:01:08.968 --> 00:01:11.203
It was like watching
a two-person performance

00:01:11.203 --> 00:01:14.841
of "12 Angry Men"
where one actor played one part

00:01:14.841 --> 00:01:17.310
and one was mad enough
for the other 11.

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:20.279
Also, Dana, I don't think you
have to worry about being crude.

00:01:20.279 --> 00:01:22.848
Nothing you can say or do
could top that debate.

00:01:22.848 --> 00:01:26.252
Wolf Blitzer coulda shown up
in full BDSM gear,

00:01:26.252 --> 00:01:28.421
screaming the lyrics to "WAP,"
and it still wouldn't have been

00:01:28.421 --> 00:01:30.456
the crudest thing
that happened last night.

00:01:30.456 --> 00:01:32.458
Woulda been the most fun thing.

00:01:32.458 --> 00:01:34.827
You know, we got a couple
more debates left, Wolf.

00:01:34.827 --> 00:01:36.262
It was, to state the obvious,

00:01:36.262 --> 00:01:38.765
one of the most embarrassing
debacles in American history.

00:01:38.765 --> 00:01:41.100
And I'm including
Kevin Federline performance

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:43.469
at the 2016 Choice Awards.

00:01:43.469 --> 00:01:44.704
Okay, Fed,
we owe you an apology.

00:01:44.704 --> 00:01:46.305
We thought "PopoZao" was
the lowest point

00:01:46.305 --> 00:01:47.740
in American history,
but that was

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:50.977
before the president took
a PopoZao on the debate stage.

00:01:50.977 --> 00:01:52.845
And the debate somehow
managed to top

00:01:52.845 --> 00:01:54.881
